OpenSwoole: an asynchronous, coroutine-based networking framework for
PHP, the OpenSwoole fork of Swoole 4 (its 4.12 API). It has the classes
of Swoole, and PHP stops when both are loaded: its ini comes with its
line commented out (the message of the package says how to switch).

Without OpenSSL (no SSL and TLS of openswoole: SWOOLE_SSL, HTTPS, WSS),
with php83-mysqlnd; php83-openswoole-openssl has it, with
php83-mysqlnd-openssl.

PECL openswoole for php83 of azsupport/ports, built from ext/openswoole
of the release tarball of azsupport/php-src, which bundles it:
lib/php/20230831/openswoole.so, loaded by its ini in etc/php83/conf.d.
